68% of Google searches (blended mobile & desktop avg) in Similarweb's clickstream panel now end without a click. That's up 33% from when our first data point around this trend ten years ago (in 2016 with the now-defunct Jumpshot).

Thanks to the hard work of Similarweb's Adelle Kehoe and Sam Sheridan, we've published new, updated numbers on Zero Click Search in the United States, covering January-April of 2026. In this report, you'll find a comparison to the past studies, methodology details, and more of what this means for the fast-declining open web.